        <li><strong>Step 2: Intra-Region Redlock:</strong> In that home region, workers acquire Redlock across 3 to 5 independent Redis instances deployed across separate Availability Zones within that single metropolitan region (e.g., <code>us-east-1a</code>, <code>us-east-1b</code>, <code>us-east-1c</code>). Round-trip latency remains sub-3ms.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 3: Relational Backstop:</strong> The final database mutation is committed to a globally replicated database (such as AWS Aurora Global Database or CockroachDB) enforcing a strict <code>UNIQUE CONSTRAINT (gateway_event_id)</code> as the mathematical backstop.</li>
      </ul>

