      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-4">
        8. Production Anti-Patterns & Hardening Checklist
      </h2>
      <p>
        Ensure your deployment incorporates these production hardening standards:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-slate-300">
        <li><strong>Never use Redis asynchronous replication replicas as Redlock nodes:</strong> In a standard Redis master-replica setup, replication is asynchronous. If the master acknowledges a lock and crashes before replicating to the replica, failover promotes the replica, which has no record of the lock, violating mutual exclusion. Use independent master nodes.</li>
        <li><strong>NTP Clock Synchronization:</strong> Redlock relies on monotonic time. Ensure local host operating systems synchronize via Amazon Time Sync Service or Google NTP with maximum permitted clock drift under 10 milliseconds.</li>
        <li><strong>Always Return HTTP 200 on Suppressed Retries:</strong> When a concurrent duplicate webhook is suppressed by an active Redlock or a <code>PROCESSED</code> key, immediately return HTTP <code>200 OK</code> or <code>202 Accepted</code>. Returning 4xx or 5xx codes causes payment gateways to exponentially accelerate retries.</li>
      </ul>
